Start with pip install streamlit pandas plotly reportlab requests and get a bare Streamlit shell running with a sidebar nav (st.sidebar.radio) linking to placeholder pages for each module.

Phase 2: Log Analyzer first — 

Parse with pandas (regex extraction for SSH auth logs: Failed password for .* from (\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+))
Group by IP, count failures, flag if count > threshold in a time window → brute-force detection
Plotly bar chart of top offending IPs
This alone is a solid mini-project if you stop here

Phase 3: URL Checker

Regex/heuristics: IP-literal URLs, @ in URL, excessive subdomains, known shortener domains list, Levenshtein distance against a list of popular domains for typosquat detection (python-Levenshtein or difflib)
No API needed initially — score based on weighted rule hits (0–100)

Phase 4: IOC Extractor

Pure regex module: IPs, URLs, emails, domains, hashes (MD5/SHA1/SHA256 by length pattern)
Reusable — call it from the log analyzer and email analyzer output

Phase 5: Report Generator

Feed structured findings (dict/JSON) into ReportLab → PDF with sections you listed
You already have ReportLab experience from your resume project, so this should be fast for you

Phase 6: Email Analyzer

Use Pythons email module to parse .eml (headers, sender, links, attachments)
Heuristics: SPF/DKIM fail mentions, mismatched display name vs. actual address, urgency keywords, link-domain mismatch from display text

Phase 7: Hash Checker + AI Chat

Hash checker: local CSV/SQLite lookup first; VirusTotal API is a nice add-on later (needs a free API key, rate-limited)
AI chat: wrap OpenAI/Claude API call with SOC-analyst system prompt, feed it context from whichever module's output is currently loaded
